=== BOB-172 — a refused tracker must not be reported as "empty" ===
captured: 2026-08-22   branch: 002-user-owned-downloads
NOTE: no credential VALUE appears in this artifact or in any test fixture
      committed with it — variable NAMES only (§11.4.10). All test fixture
      values are synthetic placeholders, never real session material.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
ROOT CAUSE (§11.4.102) — located, not guessed
------------------------------------------------------------------------
download-proxy/src/merge_service/search.py, every private-tracker search
path (rutracker cookie path, rutracker credential path, nnmclub, kinozal,
iptorrents) did:

    async with session.get(search_url, cookies=...) as resp:
        html_content = await resp.text()      # <-- resp.status NEVER READ

The refusal body was then handed to the row parser, which found no rows and
returned []. In `_run_search`:

    stat.status = "success" if results else "empty"

so a tracker that REFUSED us was reported as `status="empty",
results_count=0, error=None`. That is the §11.4.201(6) FALSE-NULL at the
product layer: a blind instrument and a genuinely empty tracker return the
identical quiet zero, and the fan-out still "succeeds".

This is exactly the `status=empty, results_count=0 in 164ms` that TWO prior
investigations recorded as an unexplained anomaly (BOB-093 live search smoke
and the BOB-136 audit). 164ms is far too fast for a real remote search and is
entirely consistent with an immediate 403.

WHY THE PRE-EXISTING GUARD COULD NOT CATCH IT — it fails on BOTH conditions:
    if len(html_content) < 1024 and "captcha" in html_content.lower():
The measured challenge body is 5351 B (not < 1024) and carries
"Just a moment" / "cf-chl" / "challenge-platform", not "captcha".

------------------------------------------------------------------------
RED — observed BEFORE any source change (§11.4.224)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
$ .venv/bin/python -m pytest \
    tests/unit/merge_service/test_bob172_tracker_http_error_not_empty.py \
    -p no:schemathesis -q --import-mode=importlib -p no:randomly

  AssertionError: HTTP 500 folded into status='empty'
  assert 'empty' == 'error'
  AssertionError: HTTP 503 folded into status='empty'
  ...
  8 failed, 4 passed in 4.82s

The 4 that passed pre-fix are the NEGATIVE CONTROLS plus one supplementary
assertion — correct by construction: a negative control must be green both
before AND after the fix, or it is not pinning the other direction.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
GREEN — after the fix
------------------------------------------------------------------------
  12 passed in 2.14s

Fix shape (reuse-first, §11.4.28 — nothing new was minted that already
existed):
  * `_classify_upstream_http_status(status, body_sample)` returns None for
    any 2xx and a diagnostic dict otherwise, in the SAME shape
    `_classify_plugin_stderr` already returns.
  * It emits the SAME `upstream_http_403` / `upstream_http_404` tokens the
    plugin-subprocess path already emits, so both tracker paths speak ONE
    dialect rather than two divergent ones.
  * It populates `TrackerSearchStat.http_status` — a field already declared
    and already serialised by `to_dict()`, which no code path had ever
    assigned.
  * It rides the existing `_last_public_tracker_diag` side-channel that
    `_run_search` already drains. No new plumbing.
  * Body markers ("just a moment" / "cf-chl" / "challenge-platform") sharpen
    the HUMAN-READABLE reason only. The TRIGGER is the HTTP status read from
    the authoritative source (`resp.status`) — never a body-text proxy that
    something which is not the condition could satisfy (§11.4.201).

Applied to ALL FIVE private-tracker search sites, not just rutracker: the
identical false-null lived on every one of them, and fixing one while leaving
four siblings open would have left the same silent contributor in place.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
PAIRED §1.1 MUTATIONS — both directions, neither survives
------------------------------------------------------------------------
MUTATION 1 (under-fire — restores the fold-to-empty defect):
    if 200 <= status < 300:  ->  if True:   # classifier always returns None
  RESULT: 8 failed, 4 passed  — identical to the pre-fix RED split.
          The negative controls stayed GREEN, proving they do not
          accidentally depend on the fix.

MUTATION 2 (over-fire — the false-positive direction, §11.4.201(1)):
    if 200 <= status < 300:  ->  if False:  # classify even 2xx as refusal
  RESULT: 3 failed, 9 passed — ALL THREE negative controls went RED.
          test_http_200_with_zero_rows_stays_empty_and_successful
          test_http_200_with_zero_rows_carries_no_error
          test_http_200_zero_rows_is_not_in_metadata_errors

A guard that only caught mutation 1 would be half a guard. Reporting a
legitimately-empty search as an error is a FAIL-bluff of equal severity to
the false-null being fixed — it sends the operator to fix healthy code and
teaches them to ignore tracker errors, defeating the very signal this change
exists to raise.

Mutation-residue scan after restore: CLEAN (§11.4.84) — zero `MUTATED`
markers in source or tests.

MECHANISM-LEVEL GUARD (added after a self-review pass, §11.4.115(F)):
An earlier version of `test_403_body_never_reaches_the_row_parser` asserted
only on the resulting row COUNT. That passed in BOTH directions -- a challenge
page yields zero rows whether or not the guard exists -- so it discriminated
nothing and was unvalidated instrumentation. It now spies on
`_parse_rutracker_html` and asserts the refusal body never reaches it. Under
MUTATION 1 it fails with the mechanism named directly:

    AssertionError: the HTTP 403 challenge body was passed to
    _parse_rutracker_html ([6235] byte(s)).

and it carries its own negative control
(`test_healthy_200_body_DOES_reach_the_row_parser`) so a guard that skipped
the parser for EVERY response -- breaking all searches while still passing the
assertion above -- is caught too.

