STUB RECONCILIATION (§11.4.120) -- an existing test file was edited
------------------------------------------------------------------------
tests/unit/merge_service/test_nnmclub_session_login.py FAILED against the
fix with `'_FakeResp' object has no attribute 'status'`. That is a stub
modelling gap, not a product defect: a real aiohttp `ClientResponse` always
carries `.status`.

I record this prominently because "a test failed so I edited the test" is
exactly the shape a fake-pass takes. What was done and what was NOT:
  * ADDED: `status=200` default on the `_FakeResp` stub -- completing its
    model of the aiohttp contract.
  * NOT TOUCHED: every assertion in that file. They assert cookie/session
    behaviour, not status, and mean exactly what they meant before.
  * EXPLICITLY REJECTED: making the product code tolerant via
    `getattr(resp, "status", 200)`. Defaulting an unreadable status to "OK"
    is a fail-open on an unverifiable input (§11.4.252) and would re-create
    the very false-null this item exists to close. The stub was wrong; the
    guard is right.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
BLAST RADIUS (§11.4.92 Pass 2) — one deliberate behaviour change, disclosed
------------------------------------------------------------------------
`_search_one` previously returned `(name, results, None)` even when the diag
had already flipped `stat.status` to "error". So `metadata.errors` stayed
EMPTY beside an errored chip — the same false-null one layer up, in the
summary channel a caller of the merge API actually reads. It now returns the
diag's error when `stat.status == "error"`.

CONSEQUENCE THE REVIEWER MUST WEIGH, stated plainly rather than buried:
download-proxy/src/api/routes.py:727 does

    captcha_errors = [e for e in metadata.errors if "captcha" in e.lower()]
    if captcha_errors and not results: -> status="captcha_required"

Because `metadata.errors` was never populated from diag, that branch was
DEAD. It can now fire — specifically for the pre-existing `upstream_captcha`
diag, whose message contains "CAPTCHA". This appears to be the branch's
intended behaviour finally becoming reachable (it tells the operator to solve
the CAPTCHA instead of showing a bare "no results"), and it only fires when
the whole search returned zero results anyway. It is NOT triggered by this
change's own 403 messages, which contain no "captcha" substring.

I did not modify routes.py — a sibling stream is live in api/. Flagging it
for the reviewer's judgement rather than silently changing an out-of-scope
contract.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
(a) IS THE 403 PERMANENT POLICY, RATE-BASED, OR CLIENT-SIGNATURE-BASED?
------------------------------------------------------------------------
STOPPED AT A CAPABILITY BOUNDARY (§11.4.112). Recorded, not worked around.

FACT (measured, https://rutracker.org/robots.txt, one request):
  - The file is marked "BEGIN/END Cloudflare Managed content" — the site
    operator has Cloudflare's managed bot/AI-crawler blocking enabled.
  - It carries an explicit per-agent denylist:
        User-agent: ClaudeBot                      Disallow: /
        User-agent: GPTBot                         Disallow: /
        User-agent: CCBot                          Disallow: /
        User-agent: Google-Extended                Disallow: /
        User-agent: Bytespider                     Disallow: /
        User-agent: meta-externalagent             Disallow: /
        User-agent: Amazonbot                      Disallow: /
        User-agent: Applebot-Extended              Disallow: /
        User-agent: CloudflareBrowserRenderingCrawler  Disallow: /
  - For `User-agent: *` it publishes `Allow: /` with
    `Content-Signal: search=yes,ai-train=no,use=reference`, and it does NOT
    disallow /forum/tracker.php for a generic agent.

READING (§11.4.6 — what the evidence establishes, and no more):
  robots.txt and the edge are two SEPARATE enforcement layers. robots.txt
  does not forbid the search path to a generic client; Cloudflare bot
  protection refuses it at the edge regardless. So the 403 is a deliberately
  deployed edge protection, differentiated BY PATH (index open, search
  endpoint protected), not a misconfiguration on our side and not an auth
  prompt.

WHY I STOPPED HERE RATHER THAN FINISHING THE CLASSIFICATION:
  Every remaining discriminator between "permanent policy" / "rate or
  reputation scoped" / "client-signature triggered" requires varying the
  client signature to see whether the block lifts. That IS browser-signature
  evasion, which the task forbids outright — and the operator of that site
  has expressly denylisted AI-agent crawlers, this agent's class among them
  (ClaudeBot, Disallow: /). Probing for a way past a protection aimed at
  precisely this class of client is the circumvention the task's STOP
  instruction anticipates. The single permitted one-off UA variation was
  therefore NOT exercised: knowing the operator's express denylist, running
  it would have been evasion in substance whatever its packet count.
  No further requests were issued to rutracker beyond the single robots.txt
  read. No challenge was solved, no proxy rotated, no fingerprint spoofed.

VERDICT: UNKNOWN, deliberately and permanently for this agent.
  - KNOWN AS FACT: the search endpoint is refused by deliberately deployed
    Cloudflare bot protection; the refusal precedes authentication (zero
    login markers, measured 2026-08-21); credentials and fresh cookies do
    not address it.
  - UNKNOWN: whether the refusal is permanent-for-all-non-browser-clients,
    or rate/reputation scoped.
  - WHAT WOULD SETTLE IT, without anyone circumventing anything: the
    operator observing, from their OWN environment and their own client
    identity, whether an ordinary logged-in browser session reaches
    /forum/tracker.php while this service does not. That is an operator
    measurement, not an agent one. A rutracker account-level enquiry to the
    site operator is the other legitimate channel.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
(d) HONEST CAPABILITY BOUNDARY — REPORTED, NOT ACTED ON
------------------------------------------------------------------------
On the evidence above, rutracker SEARCH is not currently available to this
service, and no change within this codebase makes it available. Until that
changes, the README and merge-service documentation should stop advertising
rutracker as a live search source. Per the task's scope I did NOT edit those
docs; this is the report.

SEPARATE LATENT DEFECT SPOTTED, NOT FIXED (out of scope, reported):
`_get_enabled_trackers()` gates rutracker on RUTRACKER_USERNAME AND
RUTRACKER_PASSWORD only — it does not consider RUTRACKER_COOKIES. A
cookie-only rutracker configuration therefore never enables the tracker at
all, even though `_search_rutracker` treats cookies as the PREFERRED auth
path and the nnmclub sibling does check its *_COOKIES var. Distinct from
BOB-172; recorded so it is not lost.
